    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d857">

                <pb facs="0872" n="614" xml:id="pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 865.857An2/47</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Austro-Hungarian Chargé</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Zwiedinek</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 15, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 16</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: ...</p>
                <p>As to the <hi rendition="#italic">Ancona</hi> case, my conviction that the
                    explanation would be satisfactory has proven correct. This Embassy has not yet
                    received a direct official telegram from the Foreign Minister, and I do not know
                    as we shall get one at all, but the official announcement of the
                    Austro-Hungarian Admiralty transmitted to us by wireless via Sayville appears to
                    cover the whole situation. I enclose a copy of the telegram as we received it
                    yesterday....</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Zwiedinek</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d857-a1.xml" xpointer="d857-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
